1f9p|n|To look down upon from a place that is over or above; to look over or view from a higher position; to rise above, so as to command a view of; as, to overlook a valley from a hill. ; Hence: To supervise; to watch over; sometimes, to observe secretly; as, to overlook a gang of laborers; to overlook one who is writing a letter. ; To inspect; to examine; to look over carefully or repeatedly. ; To look upon with an evil eye; to bewitch by looking upon; to fascinate. ; To look over and beyond (anything) without seeing it; to miss or omit in looking; hence, to refrain from bestowing notice or attention upon; to neglect; to pass over without censure or punishment; to excuse.	N:1w21,6,1~1w21,6,1
